Finally managed a slashem ascension.  No interesting conducts adhered to
other than not wishing for artifacts.  Didn't polypile, but my reliance
on dipping into potions for safety meant that my unicorn horn spent some
time as a whistle.


Key here was an early magic lamp find which gave me an amulet of
unchanging.  I then spent most of the game as a crystal golem.  Had
decent luck with shops with game in that there were a lot of them,
including 2 bookstores.  I've had previous games where the mall and
minetown each had 2-3 small shops with little of interest.

Sokoban had a bag of holding, which worked out fine since I had
reflection from golemhood.


There were a few oddities about the game.  I never got crowned.  Never
saw a wand of cancellation.  There were no shrines.  I found 3 magic
lamps, 4 magic markers, and 4 gypsies.  Only used one of lamps, second
lamp was my light source for the rest of the game.   Most gypsy wishes
went for blessed potions of gain energy.  Once I got serpent's tongue I
didn't waste much more time sacrificing and praying.  I managed to buy
protection once from the minetown priest, but by the time I got back
there again I'd acquired Elvis the Vampire Mage as a pet.  Elvis took
that priest out when I was reading a spellbook.


Vampire mages make quite respectable pets.  Though I did fear leaving
them behind and having them go untame.  Eventually they got killed off
by purple worms and lurkers above.  So I genocided them along with L, Z,
h to simplify my life.


One Eyed Sam had a pretty interesting shop.  I waltzed in, went back to
crystal golem form, read a scroll of earth to wall Sam in.  Then used a
ring of conflict to thin the ranks of his helpers.  Once they were down
to just cockatrices and a giant, I took out my auto shotgun and blessed
+5 shotgun shells and blasted away.  Necromancers may be unskilled with
firearms, but Sam obligingly died twice and I took his boots of speed as
my prize.


I largely gave up on golemhood after that because I needed the higher AC
I could get from wearing heavily enchanted hawaiin shirt, robe, and
cloak.   Plus I needed the robe and helm of brilliance to get spells
like identify into castable range.  At this point was I still only level
 13, so I gain energy boosted 9 potions of extra healing up to full to
crank my hit points over 200.


My trip through the castle and gehennom was fairly uneventful until
Frankensteins lab.  Lots of gem golems there gave me a run.  Most of
them had poly trapped themselves up from credit card golems.  I
eventually managed to beat them to death and took the white coat so I
could reliably alchemize for gain level potions.  Which I then bagged
and didn't touch until the amulet run.


Once I hit the Sanctum it took me a few wasted rounds fighting things
before I stopped being stupid.  Then I got out my teleport wand and just
alternated teleporting things out of my way and casting jump to skip
forward through the gaps.  Rodney double troubled me with the high
priestess, but I just wand of deathed them a lot.  They'd managed to
summon a bunch of gem golems (significant trouble for my AC 34) so I
dipped those gain level potions into unholy water and sailed through the
ceiling with the amulet.


I used the same trick to avoid getting bogged down on the nastier maze
levels like Dispater's lair.  Picked up more teleport wands, poly wands,
death wands, scrolls of gold detection, and blank scrolls from stashes
on the way up.  Also switched amulets from reflection to flying and
refreshed my recall on variuos spells.  That wasted enough time to get
me into a few more battles with the wizard.  It was also pointless since
the only spell I bothered to cast thereafter was jumping.


Elemental levels went very smoothly until water.  Didn't even use up my
poly wand getting out of air elementals in air.  Took a really long time
and many scroll readings (thanks to the magic marker) to stumble into
the portal out of water.   So long that I had to death the wizard again
for a grand total of 7.


Once into heaven I found myself to the right of death and pestilence, so
I kept on going right towards famine.  More teleport wand and jumping
around the priests, angels, summoned insects got me through without even
fighting a single Rider.  The right side high altar turned out to be
chaotic.  No need to unpack my helm of opposite alignment!






